course: dictionary
lesson: 4074
title: Gerbils: small desert pets
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A gerbil is a small furry animal with a long tail and strong back legs. It comes from the deserts of Africa and Asia, and many people keep it as a pet. Gerbil is a noun: one gerbil, two gerbils.
explain: «Mice, rats, hamsters and gerbils all walk on four legs; hamsters have a very short tail, while mice, rats and gerbils have long ones.» So a long tail helps you tell a gerbil from a hamster.
explain: Gerbils are good at saving water, which matters in the desert. «Gerbils save water by making very dry droppings and very little urine (wee), so they drink little.»
explain: «Gerbils come from deserts where they live in tunnels, so they love a deep layer of bedding to dig in.» Gerbils are also social, so they should live in pairs or groups.
fact: A gerbil is a small furry rodent with a long tail and strong back legs.
fact: Gerbils come from the deserts of Africa and Asia.
fact: Gerbils dig tunnels and drink very little water.
fact: Gerbils drum their back feet to warn the group of danger or when they are excited.
fact: Gerbils are social, so they should live in pairs or groups.
exercise: «Gerbils come from deserts where they live in tunnels.» Where do gerbils come from? | Snowy mountains | *Deserts | The bottom of the sea | Rainforests
exercise: Gerbils «drum their back feet» to do what? | Keep their tails dry | Dig for food | *Warn the group of danger, or when they are excited | Show that they are asleep
exercise: Which animal has a very short tail, according to the sentence? | Gerbil | *Hamster | Mouse | Rat
test: Why do gerbils need very little water? | Because they have no tail | Because they live in rivers | *Because they save water with very dry droppings and very little urine | Because they never move
test: Why should a pet gerbil not live alone? | *Because gerbils are social and should live in pairs or groups | Because gerbils cannot eat | Because gerbils only sleep | Because gerbils cannot hear
exam: Which word is the plural of gerbil? | gerbil's | gerbiling | *gerbils | gerbiles
